    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0062" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg50"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 EN 3/725: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Afghanistan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kabul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-12T20:00:00+04:00">June 12, 1942—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 12—5:16 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. The following telegram has been sent to Consulate General at Beirut for
                    Minister Engert.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>June 12, 8 p.m. The Foreign Minister requested today that you be informed of
                        his most earnest hope that you will arrive in Kabul as soon as possible. He
                        stated that your early arrival is especially <pb facs="0063" n="51"
                            xml:id="pg51"/> desired in order to put an end to the abnormal situation
                        which arose, first, through the arrival of a Military Attaché prior to the
                        establishment of a Legation, and secondly, through the assignment of a
                        Secretary prior to the appointment of a Minister. He spoke at some length of
                        Afghan pride intimating that Afghan feelings had been injured by the above
                        mentioned circumstances.</p>
                    <p>Although permanent Legation quarters will not be ready for 3 months,
                        furnished temporary quarters are available now in a suburban villa.</p>
                    <p>I would therefore much appreciate being advised of your plans so that I might
                        inform the Foreign Minister accordingly.</p>
                    <p>Repeated to the Department.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thayer</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
